      "body": "Summary\r\nThis PR improves performance in parenthetical clustering by caching\r\nparenthetical tokenization, which is a hot path when grouping many\r\nsimilar parentheticals together.\r\n\r\nChanges\r\n- Adds @lru_cache to parenthetical tokenization to avoid repeated work\r\n  within a single clustering invocation\r\n- Clears the tokenization cache at the start of each clustering run to\r\n  prevent cross-request and cross-test contamination\r\n- Does not alter clustering logic, grouping behavior, or scoring\r\n\r\nPerformance\r\nA local benchmark simulating realistic repetition in parenthetical text\r\nshows a ~65× speedup in tokenization-heavy workloads (0.22s → 0.003s),\r\nwith >99.9% cache hit rates. A cache size of 4096 was sufficient to cover\r\nall repeated inputs while keeping memory usage bounded.\r\n\r\nDeployment\r\n- [x] `skip-web-deploy`\r\n- [x] `skip-celery-deploy`\r\n- [x] `skip-cronjob-deploy`\r\n- [x] `skip-daemon-deploy`\r\n",
